{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"octane-pacer"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter connects Pacer scheduling utilities to Octane state and lifecycle management. It re-exports the core package, including utility classes, stateless functions, option types, and async retrying."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/octane-pacer","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane requires Node.js 22.22.2 or newer and Octane 0.1.36."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lifecycle-and-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle and state"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call hooks at the top level of a compiled Octane component. The compiler assigns each call its own hook slot. The hook retains its utility across renders and commits the current callback and options in a layout effect. Selected state triggers rendering, and unmounting cleans up the utility. Use Octane 0.1.36; this package does not support the 0.2 line yet."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the selected state is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass a selector to subscribe only to the fields your UI reads. The underlying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store"},{"type":"text","value":" remains available for additional subscriptions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API overview"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Utility"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convenience APIs"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/batch